poem:
And down within your scented
head,
It is nothing to me, the mother
said;
And want consorts with crime;
Or braver hero died,

The wild and bright was the
gallant
My hands were tied;
But would please the weak frail
flesh;
Sharers of a thousand dusky
toilers
Where the old oak-tree;

Twas a night of dull despair,
Showed sorrow in her heart;
Men grew wild with wrathful
